keywords:
  - agent-based simulation
  - anthropology
  - archaeology
  - reproducibility
  - demography
  - migration
  - temporary mobility
  - aggregation
  - sensitivity analysis
  - identifiability
abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for deterministic
  demography, resource-constrained permanent household migration,
  evidence-grounded spatial experiments, and explicit temporary mobility and
  aggregation under declared model assumptions. Version 0.3.2 is a documentation-
  convergence maintenance release over the v0.3.1 scientific-audit implementation.
  It changes no simulation semantics or frozen scientific results; it synchronizes
  the living project documentation with the already-implemented configuration,
  stochastic-precision, long-run, structural-sensitivity, demographic-baseline,
  and identifiability/equifinality safeguards. AnthroSim is not an empirically
  validated model of human prehistory.
